  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nA dominant upper level ridge and associated strong surface high\nwill continue to influence the weather across the area into\nearly next week. Dry conditions with seasonable temperatures\nwill keep the weather pleasant across the area. There is a\nchance for patchy dense fog late tonight into Friday morning and\nsome lingering moisture gets trapped in an inversion. The fog\npotential should be isolated to areas west of I-71. In addition,\nFriday and Saturday nights will see a widespread drop in\ntemperatures into the 30s for much of the area, possibly\ntouching the upper 20s at times. This will likely result in\nwidespread frost potential both nights with isolated areas of\nfreeze potential. Both nights may need a frost/freeze headline,\nbut will wait for tomorrow to ensure trends in models persist.",
